<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="eugenol and isoeugenol biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260303222105">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-5859" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Arabidopsis thaliana col&lt;/i&gt;: Enzyme(s) that catalyzes one or more of the key reactions in this pathway were predicted in Arabidopsis thaliana col. &lt;A href=&quot;http://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; |FRAME: CPD-6481 Eugenol| and |FRAME: ISOEUGENOL| are scent volatiles of the phenylpropene type emitted by plants as attractants and in defense response. The phenylpropenes have a phenyl ring with a propenyl side chain derived from coumaryl, coniferyl and sinapyl alcohol, which are precursors of the |FRAME: PWY-361| |CITS: [17912370]|. |FRAME: CPD-6481 Eugenol| has been in the forefront of the spice trade since ancient times, the food-preserving and analgesic properties of eugenol-rich clove has led to discoveries of new nations and trade routes. The characteristic scent of basil (|FRAME: TAX-39350|) plant is due to the volatile |FRAME: CPD-6481|, produced by the enzyme eugenol synthase |CITS: [17912370]|. The antimicrobial properties of neutrophils are shown to be inhibited by |FRAME: CPD-6481| |CITS: [18215676]|. Different plants emit them in combinations of varying amounts which imparts the distinctive aromas of flowers, in |FRAME: TAX-36903| the flowers emit an equal mixture of |FRAME: CPD-6481| and |FRAME: ISOEUGENOL| giving them strong scents |CITS: [18208524]| and in |FRAME: TAX-4102| the flowers emit more |FRAME: ISOEUGENOL| and smaller amounts of |FRAME: CPD-6481| that imparts an odor similar to freshly cut herbs. The emission of these scent volatiles follows an diurnal rhythm in |FRAME: TAX-4102| reaching its maximal emission output around midnight |CITS: [17241449]|.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="PMN" />
    <Author name="zhang" />
    <Author name="hartmut" />
